      "summaryMarkdown": "**VL-1 passed.** A normalized diff of RayX `4ee806e9`'s `virtual_list/{mod.rs,geometry.rs}` against the gpux files (with `Base` removed, `gpux::` mapped to `crate::`, `rayx_diagnostics` mapped to `diagnostics`, and doc comments stripped) leaves only these differences: the `ScrollbarHandleBase` impl and its import are gone, `virtual_list_base` is now `virtual_list`, `ItemSizeLayout` is private (it is used only in a private field), and rustfmt rewrapped some lines. No logic changed. Every name VL-1 lists is `pub` and re-exported through `elements/mod.rs`, and the module has no RayX dependency. The 12 window tests run with fast mode off and cover each case VL-1 lists. Their assertions are exact (positions, ranges, offsets, sticky events, quad count), so each can fail. The c-vl-unit check counted 26 unit tests.\n\n**VL-2 passed.** `list-virtual` shows 1,000 rows of 20, 30 and 40 px with `listitem` semantics at scales 1 and 2, on every lane, the same as the sibling list scenes. Before the wheel it expects Entry 0 and Entry 3 to exist and Entry 30 and Entry 999 to be missing. After ten 90 px wheel steps it expects Entry 30 and Entry 31 to exist and Entry 0 and Entry 100 to be missing, and the capture must differ from the first. Both are registered under `Area::VirtualList` with lane A and lane C catalog entries. The lane A scene and `lane_a_fast_parity list_virtual` both passed.\n\nOne cosmetic issue, not a defect: the module doc keeps a bare Zed URL, which `rustdoc::bare_urls` would flag.",
      "findingIds": [],
      "recordedAt": "2026-10-16T18:04:05Z"
    },
