      "summaryMarkdown": "**VL-3 passes**, unchanged since the first review. The default handle lives in element state, keyed per element id, created once and tracked on the base div. `track_scroll` and `track_external_scroll` replace it, and no new publication path is added. The bounded `drew again` test covers fast mode off and on.\n\n**VL-4 passes after repair.** The cause is verified: `TaffyLayoutEngine::clear` drops closures, and `keep_retained_nodes` restores them only for text leaves. A ParentViewport list now lays itself out around a keyed spacer child of its content extent. It keeps its extent under retention and matches the old measured leaf with fast mode off in every probed case: both axes, block and flex hosts, with and without padding. s02-F1, s02-F2 and s02-F3 are resolved, and the 7-test group passes.\n\n**Follow-up risk, not this sprint:** kept non-text measured leaves are still sized empty under retention. A `uniform_list` with `Infer` sizing and auto height in a retained view gives a parent `max_offset` of 0 with fast mode on, against 19,800 off. That needs a general retention fix in a follow-up epic.\n\nThe full review is resubmitted because reopening t04 for repair dropped the boundary's failed review, so a reattestation had nothing to carry.",
